Wafer Defect Control Supports Advanced Chip Manufacturing

Crystal-originated pits can affect gate-oxide integrity, leakage performance and device isolation. As semiconductor structures become more complex, manufacturers increasingly rely on carefully controlled wafer growth and defect-management processes to improve yield and reliability.

Low COP wafers reduce the density or impact of harmful defects, while COP-free wafers aim to eliminate these defects from critical wafer regions.

Advanced Logic and Memory Create Demand

Premium wafer quality is important in logic processors, DRAM, flash memory and other devices with demanding electrical specifications. The value of defect reduction increases when a wafer has already undergone multiple expensive fabrication steps.

